<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yoshida Shōin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1830–1859</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Yoshida Shoin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yoshida Shōin (1830–1859) was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> teacher and thinker of the Chōshū domain. He tried to stow away on one of Commodore <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthew-c-perry">Perry</a>'s ships in 1854 to study the West and was imprisoned. At his small school at Hagi, the Shōka Sonjuku, he taught many future leaders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration">Meiji Restoration</a>, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ito-hirobumi">Itō Hirobumi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takasugi-shinsaku">Takasugi Shinsaku</a>, in loyalty to the emperor. He was executed in the Ansei Purge in 1859.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yoshida-shoin.jpg" alt="Yoshida Shōin" width="320" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yoshida_Shoin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
